# Git Commit Messages

When generating Git commit messages:

- Use Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `docs:`, `test:`, `chore:`, `build:`, `ci:`, etc.). Ref: https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/
- Use an optional scope matching the Go package or area changed, e.g. `feat(config):`, `build(docker):`.
- Write the commit message in English.
- Keep the first line/title under 60 characters, imperative mood, lowercase, no trailing period.
- Do not add an overly verbose body unless the change is complex.

Example: `feat(api): add health check endpoint`
